 indicates natural and artificial harmonics. Allowing the type of pitch to be specified,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"combined with controls for appearance\/playback differences, allows both the notation and the sound to be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"represented. Artificial harmonics can add a notated touching pitch; artificial pinch harmonics will usually"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not notate a touching pitch. The attributes for the harmonic element refer to the use of the circular harmonic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"symbol, typically but not always used with natural harmonics."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLHarmonic","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFont":{"title":"MXLFont","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfont","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLFont","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFont","abstract":[{"text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"font names. The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vs. a music font."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLFont","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAboveBelow":{"title":"MXLAboveBelow"